+---
+id: task-002-json-patch-rfc-6902-applypatch
+type: task
+title: "JSON Patch (RFC 6902) applyPatch"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# JSON Patch (RFC 6902) applyPatch
+
+## Request
+
+Our services need to change JSON documents with standard patches. Implement JSON Patch, as specified in
+RFC 6902, with its six operations: `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test`.
+
+Export a function `applyPatch(document, patch)` from `src/index.ts`. It applies a JSON Patch (an array of
+operations) to a JSON document and returns the resulting document as a new value: it must not mutate its
+input. It throws an error when the patch is invalid, or when one of its operations fails.
+
+Pointers in `path` and `from` are JSON Pointers (RFC 6901), as implemented by `resolvePointer`.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- The patch must be an array of operation objects. Each operation must have a known `op`, a string `path`,
+  a `value` for `add`, `replace` and `test`, and a string `from` for `move` and `copy`. Anything else throws.
+- Operations apply in order; each one sees the result of the previous one. If one fails, `applyPatch` throws.
+- `add`: sets an object member (replacing an existing one); in an array, inserts before the index, where
+  `-` appends. An array index must be at most the array length. A path of `""` replaces the whole document.
+- `remove`: removes an object member or array element. The target must exist.
+- `replace`: replaces the value at an existing target. The target must exist.
+- `move`: removes the value at `from` and adds it at `path`. `from` must exist, and must not be a proper
+  prefix of `path` (a value cannot be moved into itself).
+- `copy`: adds a copy of the value at `from` to `path`. `from` must exist.
+- `test`: throws unless the value at `path` equals `value` (deep equality, per RFC 6902 section 4.6).
+- The input document and patch are not mutated; the result shares no mutable state with the input.
+- Array index tokens follow RFC 6901: non-negative integers without leading zeros; `-` is valid only
+  where RFC 6902 allows it (`add`, and the target parent of `add`/`copy`/`move`).
+- Tests cover each operation, the error cases above, and that the input is left unchanged, with
+  `npm test` (`node --test`).
+
+## Requirement
+
+Standard: RFC 6902, JavaScript Object Notation (JSON) Patch. The library must follow the published
+standard it implements.
